      "selectedText": [
        "We estimate a spectral type of M 1\\pm 0.5 , \\mathrm{L/L_{\\odot}=-1.20\\pm 0.05} dex, and \\mathrm{T_{eff}=3700\\pm 100} K for GJ 2060 A. The B component is a M 3\\pm 0.5 dwarf with \\mathrm{L/L_{\\odot}=-1.63\\pm 0.05} dex and \\mathrm{T_{eff}=3400\\pm 100} K.",
        "Therefore, we estimate that GJ 2060 A is a M1 \\pm 0.5 dwarf.",
        "We find \\mathrm{T_{eff}=3700\\pm 100} K and log g > 4.0 dex for GJ 2060 A. Similarly, we find \\mathrm{T_{eff}=3400\\pm 100} K and log g \\geq 3.5 dex for GJ 2060 B.",
        "Parameter This work a (au) 4.03\\pm 0.03\\left(\\frac{d}{15.69\\text{ pc}}\\"
      ],
      "componentMapping": "GJ 2060 A/B = WDS 07289-3015 (HDS 1054) A/B = MSC A/B. Luminosities use the paper's adopted distance (abstract and Table 10 axis at 15.69 pc).",
      "note": "Individual masses in Tables 11-12 are evolutionary-model predictions; only the total dynamical mass is measured."
    },
